<h2>2. Choose categories that match how guests search</h2>
<p>Your <strong>primary category</strong> carries the most weight. Pick the most specific one that is true: "Mexican restaurant" beats "Restaurant," and "Ramen restaurant" beats "Japanese restaurant" if ramen is what you are known for. Then add secondary categories for what else you genuinely offer, such as "Bar," "Brunch restaurant" or "Caterer."</p>
<h3>Attributes are small but they add up</h3>
<p>Fill in every attribute that applies: outdoor seating, vegan options, wheelchair accessible entrance, reservations, delivery, happy hour. Guests filter by these, and Google uses them to match listings to searches like "patio dining near me."</p>
